\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  \textbf  {Conceptual framework of the shift-invariant  PH circuit.} (a) Relationship between different families of quantum transformations. The proposed  PH circuit belongs to the broader class of shift-invariant circuits and serves as a shallow-depth alternative to the standard quantum Fourier transform (QFT). (b) Schematic of the hidden subgroup problem (HSP) solver. Following the oracle $U_f$ evaluation, the traditional QFT block is replaced by our shift-invariant  PH circuit to extract the subgroup information before measurement.}}{1}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:illus}{{1}{1}{\textbf {Conceptual framework of the shift-invariant \myqc circuit.} (a) Relationship between different families of quantum transformations. The proposed \myqc circuit belongs to the broader class of shift-invariant circuits and serves as a shallow-depth alternative to the standard quantum Fourier transform (QFT). (b) Schematic of the hidden subgroup problem (HSP) solver. Following the oracle $U_f$ evaluation, the traditional QFT block is replaced by our shift-invariant \myqc circuit to extract the subgroup information before measurement}{figure.1}{}}
